{
  "id": "COMPOUND:4757 - PROTEIN:1106",
  "verbalization": "TG-100801 is implicated in the target pathway of the Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit gamma-2 through multiple indirect connections. The evidence suggests that TG-100801 acts as a target for Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit beta-2, which in turn is a target of several compounds, including ABT-560 and (3S,4aS,8aR)-5,8a-dimethyl-3-prop-1-en-2-yl-2,3,4,4a,7,8-hexahydro-1H-naphthalene. Additionally, TG-100801 is also linked to Asparaginase Erwinia chrysanthemi, which targets the same receptor subunit. These findings collectively imply that TG-100801 may exert its effects through a mechanism that involves the Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit gamma-2, possibly through the modulation of its downstream signaling pathways. The evidence supports a potential role for TG-100801 in targeting this receptor subunit, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated.",
